{"nodes": [{"id": "mobile_dev_plan_soundboss_mobile", "label": "SoundBoss Mobile app", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:1-8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mobile client for the SoundBoss music-group platform, reusing the web backend (Supabase project kgkghsvgwoltlnnrufop) and the same Cloudflare R2 edge functions so mobile and web stay in sync."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_expo_sdk_54_stack", "label": "Expo SDK 54 stack (RN 0.81, expo-router, New Architecture)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:9-21", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_design_system", "label": "Design system h\u00e9rit\u00e9 du web (palette, Plus Jakarta Sans)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:22-38", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tokens (charcoal, warmGold, terracotta, cream\u2026) are inherited from the web app so both clients look identical; dark theme is the default (userInterfaceStyle dark) with light mode deferred to step 13."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_supabase_client", "label": "Client Supabase RN (src/lib/supabase.ts)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:106-113", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Configured with SecureStore storage, autoRefresh and a URL polyfill; detectSessionInUrl is false because there is no browser URL to parse on native."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_securestore_session", "label": "Persistance de session dans SecureStore", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:331-332", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Auth tokens are stored in expo-secure-store and never in AsyncStorage, because AsyncStorage is unencrypted plain storage."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_tanstack_query", "label": "TanStack Query v5 (cache & data fetching)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:13", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_r2_upload", "label": "Upload Cloudflare R2 (src/lib/r2.ts)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:110-111", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reuses the web edge functions (JWT required) so there is a single upload path; React Native sends a Blob via fetch(uri) then a direct PUT, and CORS was already configured for the web client."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_image_compression", "label": "Compression d'image avant upload (src/lib/image.ts)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:110-111", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "expo-image-manipulator converts to WebP at 1600 px with a fallback to the original, to cut mobile-data usage and R2 storage cost."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_database_types", "label": "src/lib/database.types.ts (types g\u00e9n\u00e9r\u00e9s Supabase)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:339-344", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Must be regenerated after every migration via the Supabase MCP generate_typescript_types. Pitfall: the generator silently omits overloaded functions \u2014 ajouter_morceau_setlist exists with 5 and 7 arguments and disappears from the types while PostgREST still resolves the 7-argument version and tsc passes."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_auth_onboarding", "label": "Auth & onboarding 3 \u00e9tapes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:120-124", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Email+password and phone+OTP sign-in, translated error messages (erreurs.ts), session guard in the root _layout; onboarding saves per step so progress is not lost."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_boite_dialogue", "label": "Bo\u00eetes de dialogue custom (BoiteDialogue / FournisseurDialogue)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:63-64", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaces native Alert with themed confirmer/succes/erreur dialogs via a useDialogue hook, used everywhere destructive or irreversible actions occur."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_groupes", "label": "Groupes (liste, d\u00e9tail, membres, pupitres)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:132-137", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Segmented tabs (Membres, Pupitres, Projets, R\u00e9p\u00e9titions, Fichiers, Chat, Stockage) with role-gated actions \u2014 Chef/Admin/Membre badges, Stockage tab restricted to the chef."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_projets", "label": "Projets (groupe & perso, r\u00e9pertoire, avancement)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:139-148", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Global progress is the average of the repertoire; the per-song slider (0-100) uses an optimistic cache update with an edit/save icon so the value is not fought over by refetches."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_taches_projet", "label": "T\u00e2ches de projet (CRUD, statuts, assignation, \u00e9ch\u00e9ances)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:67-69", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_liaison_projets_repetitions", "label": "Liaison projets \u2194 r\u00e9p\u00e9titions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:65-67", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A rehearsal can be created from a project and carries a project badge, so rehearsal work is traceable to the project it advances; personal rehearsals get their own detail page /seances/[id]."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_repetitions", "label": "R\u00e9p\u00e9titions / s\u00e9ances (planification, RSVP, setlist, notes)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:150-160", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "RSVP has 4 statuses via rsvp_seance; the attendance sheet is read-only for plain members and editable (swipe) only by chef/admin via maj_presence."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_stats_assiduite", "label": "Stats d'assiduit\u00e9 (statistiques_presences_groupe)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:151-153", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_chat_realtime", "label": "Chat temps r\u00e9el (Realtime postgres_changes sur messages)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:162-177", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Requires the supabase_realtime publication enabled on messages plus REPLICA IDENTITY FULL (the publication was found empty). Discussion selector scopes visibility: members see the general chat plus their own pupitre, the chef sees all."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_chat_reponses", "label": "R\u00e9ponses de chat (parent_message_id)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:169-171", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The parent message is fetched in a separate query because PostgREST cannot embed a self-referential foreign key."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_chat_mentions", "label": "Mentions @ dans le chat", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:172-174", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Member ids are stored in a mentions column while the text carries @Pr\u00e9nom Nom, so highlighting survives renames and mentions can drive notifications."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_chat_edition_suppression", "label": "\u00c9dition (30 min) et suppression r\u00e9elle des messages", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:175-177", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hard delete was chosen over soft delete because RLS blocks the soft-delete update: the rewritten row would have to remain visible to pass the policy."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_mediatheque_fichiers", "label": "M\u00e9diath\u00e8que de groupe (fichiers, vue grille, modal d\u00e9tail)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:179-191", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Files target a groupe/pupitre/membre; the chef/admin sees files shared to pupitres and members via est_gestionnaire_ressource plus a client filter. Fixes: the uploader embedding had to be disambiguated (two FKs to users) and taille_bytes is now filled at upload time."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_onglet_stockage", "label": "Onglet Stockage (donut SVG des tailles par type)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:74-75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chef-only view of storage consumption per file type; it is the groundwork for the paid storage quota in the credits monetisation plan."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_invitations_par_code", "label": "Invitations par code (rejoindre_par_code)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:81-84", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A 6-digit code valid 48 h, shareable through the native Share sheet and revocable, with the deep link soundboss://rejoindre?code=123456 \u2014 lowers the friction of onboarding members who are reached by WhatsApp rather than email."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_dossiers_personnels", "label": "Fichiers personnels & dossiers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:85-88", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Five default folders (documents, loops, partitions, audios, styles) are created up front so a new musician has an obvious place to file uploads; reuses ModalDetailFichier."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_bibliotheque_ressources", "label": "Biblioth\u00e8que de ressources SoundBoss (bibliotheque_ressources)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:89-92", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resources are auto-filtered by the musician's instruments and genres; an untagged resource stays visible to everyone so curation is opt-in."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_polish_ui", "label": "Polish UI (Shimmer, Drapeau/PaysCard, BoutonDore, ModalChoix)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:93-95", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_studios", "label": "Studios (catalogue, fiche, r\u00e9servation)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:193-196", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_wallet", "label": "Wallet (solde, packs, crediter_wallet, historique)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:198-201", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only pack purchase (simulated payment) and transaction history exist; nothing consumes credits yet."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_push_client", "label": "Push client (src/lib/push.tsx, FournisseurPush)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:203-210", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mounted in app/_layout.tsx; requests permissions, creates the Android 'default' channel (importance MAX, warmGold), fetches the Expo push token with the EAS projectId. Cold-start navigation needs getLastNotificationResponseAsync in addition to addNotificationResponseReceivedListener, routed by data.url."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_device_token", "label": "Table device_token", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:206-208", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Upserted on conflict (user_id, expo_token) so one user can hold several devices; est_actif is flipped false by send-push when Expo reports DeviceNotRegistered."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_ff_enqueue_notif", "label": "ff_enqueue_notif() (SECURITY DEFINER)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:222-232", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Inserts one notifications row per recipient, reads push_dispatch_secret and supabase_functions_url from app_secrets, then net.http_post to /send-push with an X-Push-Secret header. Recipients come from membres_actifs_groupe() or membres_du_pupitre(), with the sender removed from the batch."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_triggers_notif", "label": "10 triggers AFTER INSERT/UPDATE de notification", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:216-221", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "trg_message_envoye, trg_seance_creee, trg_projet_cree, trg_projet_termine, trg_ressource_ajoutee, trg_enregistrement_ajoute, trg_setlist_ajoute, trg_groupe_membre_ajoute, trg_groupe_admin_nomme, trg_ressource_equipe_publiee, trigger_notify_ai_job_termine. They are SECURITY DEFINER and owned by postgres, so the PUBLIC revoke on ff_enqueue_notif does not break them."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_send_push", "label": "Edge function send-push", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:229-232", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "verify_jwt is false because it is called server-to-server from Postgres; it is protected by the X-Push-Secret header instead. Computes the badge as the count of unread notifications, sends to the Expo API in batches of 100, and deactivates tokens rejected as DeviceNotRegistered/InvalidCredentials."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_app_secrets", "label": "Table app_secrets (RLS USING (false))", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:233-234", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Policies deny every authenticated user (USING (false)) so only the service_role can read the push dispatch secret and functions URL."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_correctif_revoke_public", "label": "Correctif s\u00e9curit\u00e9: r\u00e9voquer ff_enqueue_notif de PUBLIC", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:235-246", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ff_enqueue_notif was executable by anon through the inherited PUBLIC grant, so anyone holding the anon key (public, embedded in the APK/IPA) could push arbitrary content to any user via /rest/v1/rpc/ff_enqueue_notif. Migrations revoke_ff_enqueue_notif_from_public_roles then revoke_ff_enqueue_notif_from_public. Trap: REVOKE FROM anon, authenticated is not enough \u2014 the privilege comes from PUBLIC; always revoke FROM PUBLIC and re-verify with has_function_privilege(), a migration's success:true proves nothing."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_serveur_non_versionne", "label": "Cha\u00eene push serveur non versionn\u00e9e dans le d\u00e9p\u00f4t", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:211-215", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "send-push and the triggers exist only on the remote Supabase project (surveyed via the Supabase MCP on 21/08); they should eventually be exported into supabase/ so the server side is reproducible from the repo."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_mode_clair_i18n", "label": "\u00c9tape 13 \u2014 Mode clair & i18n (fr/en/wo/ln)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:252-254", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Planned ThemeProvider light/dark plus strings in French, English, Wolof and Lingala for the West African target market. Not started."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_eas_build", "label": "EAS build (3 profils: development, preview, production)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:255-259", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each profile has its own update channel: development dev-client, preview internal APK, production app-bundle."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_ios_testflight", "label": "Build iOS / TestFlight (com.soundboss.app)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:259-267", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EAS credentials (distribution certificate, provisioning profile, APNs key), entitlements verified in the IPA (aps-environment production, beta-reports-active true, get-task-allow false). NSCameraUsageDescription was removed because the camera is unused, ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption false avoids the export-compliance prompt, and autoIncrement on the production profile prevents rejection for a duplicate build number. Push receipt on a TestFlight iPhone is still unconfirmed."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_expo_updates", "label": "expo-updates (runtimeVersion appVersion)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:268-270", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_offline_first", "label": "Offline-first (persistance React Query manquante)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:271-273", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "gcTime is already set to 24 h in app/_layout.tsx, but @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister + persistQueryClient are not wired yet, so the cache does not survive an app restart."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_monetisation_credits", "label": "Mon\u00e9tisation par cr\u00e9dits (pay-as-you-go)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:275-316", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "West African market: small mobile-money spends (Wave, Orange Money, MTN MoMo) rather than subscriptions, so credits are bought in packs (500-2000 FCFA, one click) and consumed per operation. Chat, push notifications, studio bookings and the marketplace stay free for retention, monetised instead through commissions (paiements, revenus_plateforme). Cost is shown and confirmed before each action. DB infrastructure exists (credit_packs, credit_tarifs, wallets, wallet_transactions, paiements, revenus_plateforme, ai_jobs, ai_creations, ressources_traitees) but nothing consumes credits yet \u2014 this is step 16, the main remaining work."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_ia_labo_audio", "label": "IA musicale & Labo Audio (tarif par op\u00e9ration)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:290-296", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-operation pricing keyed to ai_jobs / ressources_traitees: BPM/key analysis 1-2 credits as a loss-leader entry price, chord detection 3-5, audio\u2192MIDI 5-8, stem separation 15-20, mastering 10-15, pitch/time-stretch 5-10, music/lyrics/instrumental/cover generation 30-50, cover art 10."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_quota_stockage_payant", "label": "Quota de stockage payant par groupe", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:297-299", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Free quota per group (e.g. 500 Mo) then paid tiers (e.g. 1 Go = 20 credits); the chef's Stockage tab already surfaces consumption."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_crash_expo_asset", "label": "Crash au lancement des builds EAS (expo-asset hiss\u00e9)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:347-364", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The preview APK opened on the splash then closed. Cause: expo-audio@1.1.1 declares expo-asset: \"*\" as an unbounded peerDependency, so npm auto-peer-install pulled the latest published expo-asset (57.0.11, a future SDK line) and hoisted it to the node_modules root while SDK 54 expects ~12.0.13. Autolinking bound the hoisted version and the native side crashed at React init with NoClassDefFoundError: expo.modules.kotlin.types.AnyTypeCache from AssetModule.kt:125 \u2014 a class absent from expo-modules-core@3.0.30. Fix: pin expo-asset as a direct dependency (~12.0.13) to dedupe the tree. Lesson: npx expo install --check does not catch this (it only inspects direct dependencies); run npm ls expo-asset after every npm install and distrust \"*\" peers. Reproducible without a phone: adb install the EAS APK on an emulator and read adb logcat for FATAL EXCEPTION."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_rpc_convention", "label": "Convention RPC SECURITY DEFINER {success, message, data}", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:337-338", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The mobile app reuses the web's SECURITY DEFINER functions unchanged, all returning the same JSON envelope, so business rules live in one place."}, {"id": "mobile_dev_plan_commandes_utiles", "label": "Commandes utiles (start, ios, android, lint, prebuild)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "mobile_dev_plan.md", "source_location": "mobile_dev_plan.md:318-327", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "npx expo install <pkg> is prescribe